# Operator dashboard

The UI is a presentation layer. Detection, tracking, association, and compliance stay in the Python pipeline.

- Contract: `ProcessedFrame.scene_summary` + confirmed `PPEViolationEvent`. API must not re-run association or zone rules. React must not derive helmet/mask/vest/overall from raw boxes.
- Live view is JPEG polling (`data/live/{camera_id}.jpg` or in-memory buffer), not RTSP in the browser. Poll via `usePoll` / `dashboard.poll_interval_ms`.
- Routes: `/dashboard`, `/events`, `/events/:id`, `/cameras`. Vite proxies `/api` → `http://127.0.0.1:8000`.
- Never return `rtsp_url` or passwords. Validate ids with `is_safe_camera_id` / `is_safe_event_id`. Evidence by event id with path-traversal checks (`src/api/paths.py`).
- `MOCK_DATA=true` must stay labeled **DEVELOPMENT MODE — live counts are simulated**. Mock events have no evidence files.
- CORS stays local dashboard origins; methods GET-only unless a new write API is explicitly requested.
- Styling: reuse CSS variables in `frontend/src/index.css` (`--safe`, `--attention`, `--warn`, `--panel`). Control-room dark UI, high contrast. Do not introduce a new design system.
- SQLite (`data/ppe.sqlite`) stores event metadata only. No image blobs, no one-row-per-frame.
